senses
  entry
    definition "a state of extreme poverty"
    id oewn-14517010-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (privation deprivation neediness)
  entry
    definition "the state of needing something that is absent or unavailable"
    examples ("there is a serious lack of insight into the problem" "water is the critical deficiency in desert regions" "for want of a nail the shoe was lost")
    id oewn-14472871-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (lack deficiency)
  entry
    definition "anything that is necessary but lacking"
    examples ("he had sufficient means to meet his simple needs" "I tried to supply his wants")
    id oewn-09390888-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (need)
  entry
    definition "a specific feeling of desire"
    examples ("he got his wish" "he was above all wishing and desire")
    id oewn-07501369-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (wish wishing)
  entry
    definition "feel or have a desire for; want strongly"
    examples ("I want to go home now" "I want my own room")
    id oewn-01829179-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (desire)
  entry
    definition "have need of"
    examples ("This piano wants the attention of a competent tuner")
    id oewn-01191258-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (need require)
  entry
    definition "hunt or look for; want for a particular reason"
    examples ("Your former neighbor is wanted by the FBI" "Uncle Sam wants you")
    id oewn-01319724-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "wish or demand the presence of"
    examples ("I want you here at noon!")
    id oewn-00711034-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "be without, lack; be deficient in"
    examples ("want courtesy" "want the strength to go on living" "flood victims wanting food and shelter")
    id oewn-02638648-v
    partOfSpeech v
